<title>ROMANIA: Romania 91-day T-bill issue undersubscribed.</title>
<headline>Romania 91-day T-bill issue undersubscribed.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's central bank said on Thursday that the issue of 224.91 billion lei worth of three-month treasury bills was undersubscribed, with banks' bids being 41.1 billion lei below the offer.</p>
<p>The T-bills maturing on January 23, 1997 were offered with a coupon giving an annual yield of 50.15 percent.</p>
<p>Four banks --  Banca Comerciala Romana SA,  Banc Post SA, Banca Romana pentru Dezvoltare SA and  Casa de Economii si Consemnatiuni -- and their corporate clients bought the Finance Ministry's papers.</p>
<p>Another public subscription for fresh 91-day bills is scheduled on Friday when about 119 billion lei will be offered.</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 ($=3,332 lei)</p>
